## 13. SSH Remote Management

SSH version 2 was enabled for remote administration.

The management domain was standardized as:

```text
noc.lab
```

A local privileged administrative account was created and VTY access restricted to SSH.

Relevant configuration includes:

```text
ip domain name noc.lab
ip ssh version 2

line vty 0 4
 login local
 transport input ssh

line vty 5 15
 login local
 transport input ssh
```

Remote SSH access was successfully validated to both `RTR-01` and `SW-01`.

### Legacy SSH Compatibility

The physical Cisco equipment runs an older IOS release that offers legacy SSH cryptographic algorithms.

Modern Windows OpenSSH rejected the initial connection because no mutually supported key-exchange algorithm was available.

After explicitly permitting compatible legacy algorithms on the lab workstation, SSH connectivity succeeded.

This was documented as a **lab compatibility requirement**, not a configuration failure.

The experience also demonstrated the difference between:

- IP reachability
- TCP port availability
- SSH service availability
- Cryptographic negotiation
- User authentication

A device can therefore be reachable on the network while an SSH session still fails during protocol negotiation.

